    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i've been trying out box breathing lately to help with anxiety. can u explain what's actually happening to my body when i do that? like how does it affect my nervous system or cortisol?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing, or square breathing, is a fantastic technique for calming the nervous system. It works by deliberately slowing your breath, which sends a signal to your brain that you are safe, helping to counteract the \"fight or flight\" response. This process directly influences your autonomic nervous system, shifting it from sympathetic dominance (stress mode) toward parasympathetic dominance (rest and digest mode). As a result, your heart rate naturally slows down, and your body begins to lower levels of stress hormones like cortisol.",
      "source": "target",
